From a13cdc2b022065021a3185f6367de74186fcbc0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sadosystems <noreply@rargo.invalid>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 01:20:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] rargo: crate hash independent of byte positions and of
 private bodies

The crate hash (SVH) is derived from the encoded metadata. Three things made
it change on edits no dependent can observe:

- Span byte offsets were part of the hashed bytes. They are now written with
  a fixed width and left out of the hash; what a dependent can observe of a
  span (file, line and column of both ends) is hashed instead.
- The source-file tables (content hash, line table) were hashed. They are now
  encoded last and left out; the identities of the files are hashed.
- The hash of the whole HIR was folded in. Only items that leave no trace in
  the metadata (global assembly) are folded in now.

The metadata header's seventh byte is 1 to mark the format.
